---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
const updated = 'October 26, 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What spookybear2026.com collects (very little), why, and what it never does with it.">
  <article class="wrap privacy">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: this is a one-person fan site, paid for out of pocket. It collects the bare minimum needed to
      know the site works, and nothing about you is ever sold, shared for marketing, or used to target you.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What’s collected</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Basic analytics</strong> (Google Analytics 4). Page views and a handful of anonymous interaction
          counts, such as how many people tapped a filter or saved an event, so I can tell what’s useful. IP
          anonymisation is on, there is no advertising or remarketing, and Google Signals is off. It runs in a
          background worker so it never slows the page down.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Error monitoring</strong> (Sentry, free tier). If the site throws a JavaScript error in your browser,
          the error message, the page URL and your browser version are sent so I can fix it. No session replays, no
          personal details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Feedback form.</strong> If you send a correction or bug report, your message and the optional links
          you include become a public issue on GitHub. If you add an email address it is <em>not</em> published; it’s
          kept only so I can reply, and it isn’t used for anything else.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting logs.</strong> The site is served by Vercel, which keeps standard, short-lived server logs
          (request paths, IP addresses) as every host does.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <p>
        “My favs”, the day you last picked, and the filters you set live only in your browser’s local
        storage. They never leave your device and I can’t see them. Clear your browser data and they’re gone.
      </p>

      <h2>What never happens</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts, no sign-up, no email list.</li>
        <li>No selling, renting or sharing data with anyone.</li>
        <li>No advertising, retargeting, or cross-site tracking of any kind.</li>
        <li>No fingerprinting, no replaying your session.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics sets its own first-party cookies to tell returning visitors from new ones. Nothing else on
        the site sets a cookie. If you block analytics with a content blocker, everything still works.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:me@salemghoweri.com?subject=spookybear2026.com%20privacy">Email me</a> or
        <a href={`${SITE.repo}/issues`} rel="noopener" target="_blank">open an issue</a>. Last updated {updated}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-top: 24px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
</style>
